+  // content::kChromeUIResourcesHost) a second time from here would NOT
+  // merge into that source — URLDataManagerBackend keys data sources by
+  // name in a flat map (url_data_manager_backend.cc), so a second
+  // CreateAndAdd call would silently REPLACE the real chrome://resources/
+  // source and break every other WebUI page in the process. Confirmed
+  // (content/browser/webui/web_ui_data_source_impl.cc StartDataRequest)
+  // that an unmapped resource path fails closed — GotDataCallback.Run
+  // (nullptr) — not a crash, so the practical effect on this throwaway
+  // preview page is that @font-face requests for the 5 woff2 files 404
+  // and the browser falls back to a system font for the typography
+  // section; token swatches, icon glyphs, and the state matrix are
+  // unaffected. Wiring the shared origin is left as an explicit follow-up
+  // (documented in 14-07-SUMMARY.md) rather than done as an unscoped,
+  // unreviewed change to the core WebUI resource bundle.
